# Specialist routing

When a task clearly belongs to a Nova specialist, prefer that subagent over general-purpose. Wiring metadata (invoke phrases, dashboards, handoffs) lives in `.cursor/agent-system/registry.json` — do not duplicate full agent prompts here.

## Defaults

| Need | Agent | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|
| Product change verification (pytest / Vitest / Playwright / browser) | `tester` | After code changes; before claiming done |
| Maintainability / danger audit (file limits, secrets, swallows, deps) | `maintainer` | Read-only; significant diffs |
| Full-repository security posture + SEC-NNN | `security-sentinel` | Not for PR/diff review |
| Docs, MDC rules, agent prompts, canvases | `nova-agent` | Dashboard = Nova Home |
| Warrior Trading authenticated site / Day Trade Dash navigation | `warrior` | Dashboard = `agent-warrior`; not Nova Home |
| PR / branch / uncommitted diff security | Cursor `security-review` | Built-in; never swap with security-sentinel |

## Invoke

Use each agent's registered phrases from the registry (also listed in the agent spec under **Invoke phrases**). Example: “Use the tester subagent to verify …”

## Lifecycle

Every Nova specialist report must end with:

```text
**Lifecycle:** memory=unchanged|changed | promotion=none|<what> | dashboard=clean|refresh-required | handoff=none|<sibling|parent>
```

The `subagentStop` hook (`.cursor/hooks.json`) may remind once if the footer is missing. It is fail-open and never edits files.

